# This file will teach you how to setup a local IAM environment utilizing Oracle's VirtualBox (or whichever virtualization software you prefer)

# For my setup I am utilizing a desktop computer and laptop. The desktop computer has 64gb of RAM and 16-Core CPU. This will be enough storage and processing to allow
me to setup a domain controller and database server on my local network. My laptop which only has 16gb of RAM and 14-Core CPU will serve as the client for my IAM environment

# Ensure you have at least 32gb of RAM and 10-Core CPU as the domain controller and database server will require a bit of storage and processing power. If you have
a powerful enough machine and can do this on one then that is okay too. 

# The IAM environment will be built utitlizing only Windows OS. I cannot support other OS at this time (Linux, macOS, etc.)

# I will be utilizing MS VS Code for Windows. Can be downloaded here --> https://code.visualstudio.com/download?_exp_download=d53503e735

# Step 1 
Download latest version of Oracle Virtualbox for Windows hosts from here https://www.virtualbox.org/wiki/Downloads onto to host of your choosing

# Step 2 
Verify installation of Oracle Virtualbox was successful. I will open up VS Code (you can use any code editor of your choosing) and open a terminal to verify.
Navigate to "C:\Program Files\Oracle\VirtualBox\VBoxManage.exe". If it cant be found try navigating to your C: drive and then going into Program Files and look for Oracle folder.
When VirtualBox is downloadeded it will automatically create and install it here in Program Files unless explicitly written otherwise during the initial installation step. 

